  <!--
  Existing tree data tuning: Nuclear Assault (base nodes; tree not replaced)

  - Base data bug: a Contract Manager is linked to its Recruit node by a shared
    Tag (Siege City Assault uses "Initial recruits" on both). Here node 7's
    contract (DefnId 0) was tagged "Present Value", the Recruit node's Recruit
    Value, so no contract was ever placed ("Contract for: NONE" in
    AI_Operation.csv). Tag it like node 8's Contract ID so the operation can
    order a Bomber, Jet Bomber or Nuclear Submarine (Turn Limit stays 10).
  - Allow Stealing (DefnId 6) on both Recruit nodes, 8 (initial) and 13
    (ongoing). With the operation's priority 5 (above), the operation can take
    one delivery unit from a running siege (Bombers, Nuclear Submarines) or
    from City Defense's naval team (Nuclear Submarines; City Defense already
    excludes bombers).
  - These only help together with the -5 strength advantage in
    AiOperationTeams; without it a recruited Bomber still fails readiness.
  The "Will use nukes" check is unchanged: it already passes against a major
  war enemy once the war score is negative.
  -->
  <TreeData>
    <Update>
      <Where DefnId="0" NodeId="7" TreeName="Nuclear Assault" />
      <Set Tag="Initial Recruits" />
    </Update>
    <Row DefnId="6" NodeId="8" TreeName="Nuclear Assault" DefaultData="true" />
    <Row DefnId="6" NodeId="13" TreeName="Nuclear Assault" DefaultData="true" />
  </TreeData>

